Issue signed, expiring Composery sessions.

authenticated() stops comparing a password hash carried in the cookie and
validates an opaque signed token instead (overlay src/node/session.ts), so a
session expires on its own and every session dies when the password changes.

The cookie's scope stops coming from the page. Upstream derived Path and
Domain from a base/href the client sends with the request, which put two
things wrong at once: the workbench mount is the wrong scope, because this
same server answers /proxy and /absproxy above it and the browser never sent
the cookie there; and a caller that picks the Domain can widen its own session
to a parent domain. One fixed origin-root scope fixes both, makes setting and
clearing symmetric (a session created through Composery sign-in is now
actually cleared by Sign Out), and lets base/href go entirely.

